src/port/generic
================

Nothing in this folder comes from another project. memcpy.c, memmove.c,
memset.c and memcmp.c are libterae's own, under libterae's licence, given at
the top of each.

The other folders of src/port include one of them through a port_<name>.c
where they have no assembly for that function: each folder's NOTICE says
which, and why. PORT=generic builds all four, for a processor that has no
folder. They copy, fill and compare one byte at a time, so they need
nothing of the processor and are as slow as a loop of bytes can be.


Processors with no folder, and what was looked at
-------------------------------------------------

These are processors for which no memcpy, memmove, memset or memcmp in
assembly was found under a licence libterae can ship. The search took in
newlib, picolibc, NetBSD, OpenBSD, FreeBSD, NuttX, musl, klibc, Zephyr,
the vendors' public repositories and a general search. "GPL" below means
the GPL, the LGPL, or the GPL with a linking or runtime exception, none of
which allows the commercial licence.

V850, RH850       newlib and picolibc have only setjmp. Linux's is GPL.

78K0R, RL78       newlib and picolibc have only setjmp for RL78. GCC's
                  libgcc for RL78 is GPL.

Fujitsu FR        newlib and picolibc have only setjmp for fr30.
(MB91460)         Fujitsu's Softune library is proprietary.

F2MC-16FX         No GCC port exists, and no assembly was found outside
(MB96340)         Fujitsu's proprietary Softune.

HCS12, S12(X)     GCC 4.6's libgcc for m68hc11 has memcpy and memset, under
                  the GPL. GEL is LGPL. newlib has only setjmp.

PIC (8-bit,       SDCC's are C under the GPL with a linking exception.
PIC24, dsPIC)     Microchip's XC8 and XC16 libraries ship only as binaries.
                  PIC32 is MIPS32: see src/port/mips.

8051, 8052        SDCC's memset has 8051 assembly, under the GPL with a
                  linking exception.

MicroBlaze        newlib, picolibc and Xilinx's newlib have only string
                  functions in C. Linux's fastcopy.S and uClibc's copies of
                  it are GPL.

Nios II           newlib and picolibc have only setjmp. Altera's HAL has no
                  memory functions. Linux's are C under the GPL or LGPL.

Cortus APS and    Nothing is public: the Cortus GCC port was never merged,
FP cores          and Cortus offers no downloads.

MSP430, MSP430X   newlib and picolibc have only setjmp and small printf
                  helpers. mspgcc's msp430-libc has these functions in C.

AVR32             Atmel's newlib port had a memcpy.S under a BSD licence,
                  but it survives only inside a 2009 patch in crosstool-ng,
                  was never published as a file, and nothing on the machine
                  libterae is developed on assembles AVR32. uClibc's and
                  Linux's are GPL.

H8/300H, H8S      newlib's h8300 memcpy.S and memset.S carry no notice, and
                  newlib's COPYING.NEWLIB doesn't say which of its licences
                  applies to a file without one. picolibc's copies carry a
                  1990 University of California notice that requires the
                  documentation of any distribution to acknowledge the
                  University, a duty the GPL doesn't allow to be added.


clang targets MSP430, and src/ is checked with this folder on
msp430-none-elf. Nothing here targets the others, and nothing has run on
any of them.
